<title>SWITZERLAND: ALPINE SKIING-AAMODT WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP GIANT SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-AAMODT WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP GIANT SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>ADELBODEN, Switzerland 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kjetil Andre Aamodt of Norway won a men's Alpine ski World Cup giant slalom race on Tuesday in a time of two minutes 23.52 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Michael von Gruenigen of Switzerland was second in 2:23.69 and Austrian Andreas Schifferer was third with a time 2:23.96.</p>
